      "content": "#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n#include <string.h>\n#include <math.h>\n\n#define N_ITER 10 // number of simulation iterations\n#define DT 0.01f // time step\n#define SOFTENING 1e-9f // to avoid zero divisors\n#define PARALLEL_MIN_BODIES 128\n\n/*\n * Each body holds coordinate positions (i.e., x, y, and z) and\n * velocities (i.e., vx, vy, and vz).\n */\ntypedef struct { float x, y, z, vx, vy, vz; } Body;\n\n/*\n * All threads in the current team enter this work-sharing routine.\n * Each target body's force accumulation retains ascending source order.\n * The implicit barrier completes all force reads before positions change.\n */\nstatic void body_force_workshare(Body *p, float dt, int n) {\n#ifdef _OPENMP\n#pragma omp for schedule(static)\n#endif\n  for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n    float fx = 0.0f;\n    float fy = 0.0f;\n    float fz = 0.0f;\n\n    for (int j = 0; j < n; j++) {\n      float dx = p[j].x - p[i].x;\n      float dy = p[j].y - p[i].y;\n      float dz = p[j].z - p[i].z;\n      float sqrd_dist = dx*dx + dy*dy + dz*dz + SOFTENING;\n      float inv_dist = 1 / sqrt(sqrd_dist);\n      float inv_dist3 = inv_dist * inv_dist * inv_dist;\n\n      fx += dx * inv_dist3;\n      fy += dy * inv_dist3;\n      fz += dz * inv_dist3;\n    }\n\n    p[i].vx += dt*fx;\n    p[i].vy += dt*fy;\n    p[i].vz += dt*fz;\n  }\n}\n\n/*\n * Compute the gravitational impact among all pairs of bodies in\n * the system. Preserve a standalone entry point for individual calls.\n */\nvoid body_force(Body *p, float dt, int n) {\n#ifdef _OPENMP\n#pragma omp parallel if(n >= PARALLEL_MIN_BODIES)\n#endif\n  {\n    body_force_workshare(p, dt, n);\n  }\n}\n\n/*\n * Read a binary dataset with initilized bodies.\n */\nBody* read_dataset(int *nbodies) {\n  int b = fread(nbodies, sizeof(*nbodies), 1, stdin);\n  if (b != 1) {\n    fprintf(stderr,\"\\nError reading nbodie value\\n\");\n    exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n  }\n  Body *bodies = (Body *)malloc(*nbodies * sizeof(Body));\n  b = fread(bodies, *nbodies * sizeof(Body), 1, stdin);\n  if (b != 1) {\n    fprintf(stderr,\"\\nError reading input values\\n\");\n    exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n  }\n\n  return bodies;\n}\n\n/*\n * Write simulation results into a binary dataset.\n */\nvoid write_dataset(const int nbodies, Body *bodies) {\n  int b = fwrite(bodies, nbodies * sizeof(Body), 1, stdout);\n  if (b != 1) {\n    fprintf(stderr,\"\\nError writing to output\\n\");\n    exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n  }\n}\n\nint main(int argc,char **argv) {\n  int nbodies;\n\n  Body *bodies = read_dataset(&nbodies);\n\n  /*\n   * Reuse one team across all iterations. Each work-sharing loop ends\n   * with a barrier, separating force evaluation and position updates.\n   */\n#ifdef _OPENMP\n#pragma omp parallel if(nbodies >= PARALLEL_MIN_BODIES)\n#endif\n  {\n    for (int iter = 0; iter < N_ITER; iter++) {\n      body_force_workshare(bodies, DT, nbodies);\n\n#ifdef _OPENMP\n#pragma omp for schedule(static)\n#endif\n      for (int i = 0; i < nbodies; i++) {\n        bodies[i].x += bodies[i].vx * DT;\n        bodies[i].y += bodies[i].vy * DT;\n        bodies[i].z += bodies[i].vz * DT;\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  write_dataset(nbodies, bodies);\n\n  free(bodies);\n\n  exit(EXIT_SUCCESS);\n}\n",
      "path": "src/nbody.c"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Static work sharing over independent target bodies should accelerate the quadratic force calculation on four cores without reordering force sums. Reusing one team across all ten iterations should reduce parallel-region overhead.",
